-- The two joins of a quantified obligation, on the BPMN exporter.
--
-- `the tenancy` is the BARRIER: every tenant signs, and when the last of them
-- has, one delivery follows. `receipts` is the FORK: each tenant who pays gets
-- a receipt of their own. They are the reference page's own pair
-- (doc/reference/regulative/every-run-example.l4) with the traces left out.
--
-- Until 2026-09-15 these two lowered to byte-identical BPMN and a
-- byte-identical fidelity report: L4.StateGraph.extractDeonton never read
-- Deonton.join, so the exporter could not tell them apart and the report that
-- exists to list the losses did not list this one. Now the task is a parallel
-- multi-instance activity (P-CAST says its cardinality is a run-time fact),
-- the barrier is that activity's own completion, and the fork — which BPMN
-- can only draw with a multi-instance subProcess this exporter does not emit
-- — is reported as P-FORK. The two goldens are the witness that the pair
-- stays distinguishable.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Pay     HAS payer  IS AN Actor, payee IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER
    Receipt HAS issuer IS AN Actor, to    IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
carol       MEANS Tenant OF "Carol"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob, carol

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5)
        LEST   BREACH

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`receipts` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Pay (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY theLandlord) amount
        WITHIN 7
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord
                    MUST   Receipt (EXACTLY theLandlord) (EXACTLY t) (EXACTLY amount)
                    WITHIN 5)
        LEST   BREACH BY t

-- PROBES for the ground truth of etc/lts-reader-proxy/tenancy. Everything
-- above is jl4/examples/bpmn/tenancy.l4 verbatim. The proxy position is the
-- outset of `receipts` (clock 0, nothing has happened); each #TRACE adds
-- events to it.

-- Q2/Q5: Alice pays at 3 -> the landlord owes her a receipt within 5 (by 8);
-- Bob and Carol still owe their payments by 7.
#TRACE receipts AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 3

-- Q2: any amount counts, even 0 (the rule binds `amount`, it does not test it).
#TRACE receipts AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 0 AT 3

-- Q2: paying somebody other than the landlord does not count.
#TRACE receipts AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice bob 100 AT 3

-- Q2: paying on the deadline day (7) counts.
#TRACE receipts AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 7

-- Q3: nothing by 7; the next event is at 8 -> breach, named to Alice.
#TRACE receipts AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 8

-- Q3: Alice pays late (8) -> breach, named to Alice.
#TRACE receipts AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 8

-- Q5: Alice pays at 3, no receipt by 8 -> the landlord is in breach.
#TRACE receipts AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 9

-- Q5: Alice pays at 3, receipt at 8 -> Alice's branch done; Bob and Carol
-- still owe by 7 -- so at 8 they are already late and the contract is in breach.
#TRACE receipts AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord alice 100 AT 8

-- Q5: all three pay, all three receipts -> fulfilled.
#TRACE receipts AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord 100 AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Pay bob   theLandlord 200 AT 2
  PARTY carol DOES Pay carol theLandlord 300 AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord alice 100 AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord bob   200 AT 5
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Receipt theLandlord carol 300 AT 6
